        <briefdescription>
<para>Returns monotonic array of longitudes s.t., lon_strt &lt;= lon(:) &lt; lon_strt+360. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This may require that entries be moved from the beginning of the array to the end. If no entries are moved (i.e., if lon(:) is already monotonic in the range from lon_start to lon_start + 360), then istrt is set to 0. If any entries are moved, then istrt is set to the original index of the entry which becomes lon(1).</para><para>e.g., <verbatim>   lon = 0 1 2 3 4 5  ...  358 359; lon_strt = 3
</verbatim> ==&gt; lon = 3 4 5 6 7 8 ... 359 360 361 362; istrt = 4 </para>        </detaileddescription>
